{"kind":"report","text":"No findings. Approved exact 685c068bf7bf4323ef27bf0449e7d39aa1b1edfb for implementation request #9560 (3da1d82b), against all 15 assigned artifacts, with packages/room/README.md as primary.\n\nBoth P2 findings in review 5b7aa2ba are answered. Publication's registry acquisition is inside the failure handler, so throwing and not-bound answers on a cold instance record the same capped retry schedule while remaining fail closed; a forced not-bound publication still answers forbidden. The parallel pre-engine landing lookup/read now also records a retry fence instead of repeatedly scheduling an already accepted operation at once. The landing engine retains its own retries after it is reached.\n\nLoop backoff is now a fixed set of durable per-kind due times. runAll checks them at execution, so an earlier alarm for a lease, notification or job runs that other work without retrying a failed pin. nextAlarm combines each due time with the other work and the landing engine's due time; skipped landing does not lose its retry fence. I independently reran both original reproductions, which pass. A third independent control evicts the object after the pin's failure, reloads its stored due time, runs an earlier lease alarm, confirms the pin is untouched and the lease expires, then confirms the pin retries at its due time. That also passes. The one changed pre-existing test advances to the actual next alarm after a failed canonical read rather than forcing a retry at the same instant; its original landing/result checks remain.\n\nThe original fix remains supported: checkpoint-only unpublished suffixes do not trigger publication; a healthy settled room writes no rows or alarms across the idle controls; real later entries still publish; retries double from 5 seconds to a 5-minute cap and reset after success. Canonical NOT_FOUND is separately confirmed before stopping canonical work. One admin-visible repository-gone duty remains open until confirmed publication. Pending cohorts, pins, unresolved operations and owed cleanup are kept without guessed settlement. Workspace provisioning now also waits while the canonical repository is gone, while lease expiry and the existing independent workspace/snapshot/job cleanup schedules remain available.\n\nArchitecture: the affected Artroom layers are Room's SQLite metadata, alarm scheduler and canonical publication/landing orchestration, plus the contract/admin projection and UI. The changed normative rules are documented in docs/protocol.md at this same published head: checkpoint-only publication and repository-gone behavior; the AttentionWhy extension, projection and UI agree. These are the conditions explicitly commissioned by the effective planner request. No Gitseq storage, sequencing-kernel, host-binding or Workroom interpretation contract changes. room.ts no longer needs the separate loopSettled call because runAll now owns it; relative to current comparison base 99cc4044, room.ts is unchanged. The bounded six-kind state avoids a global backoff that would stall unrelated work.\n\nSecurity: the effective request is planner's direct commission to builder for this fix, with the existing builder promise and independently inspected review assignment. Planner's operator/ratifier authority remains recorded in the workroom. This head grants no new member or credential authority. Binding failures do not permit publication or landing; the canonical-missing probe does not treat another error or a missing answer as proof of absence. Stored retry state is internal metadata, not caller-controlled scheduling authority. The diagnostics repair from main 99cc4044 is preserved: thrown failures are logged through the safe boundary; already diagnosed ArtroomErrors and ordinary forbidden binding answers are not logged twice. No unresolved security defect found.\n\nSimplification: accept one publication failure handler and one durable retry map checked by runAll and nextAlarm. Keeping the engine's own backoff separate avoids two retry schedulers for the same push. The small fixed list is justified by different work and failure boundaries. Keep commit-triggered first work prompt and unrelated alarms independent. No additional policy machinery or duplicated counter table is needed.\n\nIndependent validation: clean checkout /tmp/artroom-checker-idle-v2 at the exact head, full merge-base diff and complete v1-to-v2 repair delta examined, all 15 effective artifacts independently inspected. Dependency installation completed. Root typecheck exit 0; root npm test exit 0: 2,181 passed, one skipped, including Git Node 225, Room Node 197 and Room workerd 457. Git worker tests exit 0, 10 passed. Room Wrangler dry build exit 0. git diff --check passed and the tracked pristine checkout is clean. All 31 supplied mutations were applied individually in a disposable clone; each caused named runtime test failures, with zero syntax/load failures and zero survivors. Restored source passes the 39 selected idle/phase2b controls, exit 0, and its checkout is clean. The three independent checker controls pass, exit 0. Logs: /tmp/artroom-checker-idle-v2-{types,root,workers,dry,controls,mutants,restored}.log; mutation records: /tmp/artroom-checker-idle-v2-mut/results.json. The launcher hit transient open-file limits on some new process starts; the completed gates above ran to exit 0 and were read, and no killed or failed launcher was counted as a passing gate.\n\nLive evidence is carried explicitly, not presented as a new deployment: the four billing JSON files, smoke archive and deployment note are byte-identical to v1, verified by an exact diff. Their provider windows and per-object sums were independently checked in the v1 review: 6,289 writes before, 554 during transition, 493 in the window still overlapping smoke, then zero writes in the quiet 19:47-to-20:47 window; the last window's two reads/requests are Registry probes. The archived smoke has all 91 steps OK and completed cleanup with zero unresolved operations or repositories left. Those archives concern the recorded earlier spike deployment, not an independently queried or deployed 685c068b. The unchanged checkpoint/gone fix and repaired runtime retry fences have the independent real-DO controls above. No new live provider call or deployment was performed by checker.\n\nMain has advanced to 7be42275 with Mint A, which is not in this candidate; preserve it on landing. Mint B/C also touch core.ts and must retain this head's per-kind retry rules at their independently reviewed combined head. This verdict closes only the idle-write implementation at a sealed landing; it does not close the larger row-cost commission, its outstanding isolated measurements/redaction/accounting findings, pending-pin experiment, or the other proposed budgets. Only ALARM is enforced here; attention/idempotency caps remain separate work. Full functional scope remains open.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:42881f5669287fecd1bb71b5b6c611709e0ea6d6","binding":"assigned","head":"685c068bf7bf4323ef27bf0449e7d39aa1b1edfb","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a64f43b6c766dc9c2bb2111353f25e0312fb2b33\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13eb467700080dba5b51d6a8357c4503c6fe9286\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a64f43b6c766dc9c2bb2111353f25e0312fb2b33","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}